Synchronous: Synchronous code will be executed line by line and it will block the next lines 
until previous lines are executed completely.
Asynchronous: Asynchronous code does not block execution. It starts an operation and allow the program 
to continue executing other statments while waiting for the operation to complete.


// playwright browser actions uch a click, fill and goto are Asynchronous because they involve communication
with the browser and can take time to complete. Therefore they return Promises. and we use await to 
make sure the next step does not execute until the current action finishes.


